    "general_clue_0": "There was exactly one person on a carpet.",
    "clue_custom_text1": "There was exactly one person on a carpet.",
    "clue_custom_text2": "",
    "clue_custom_text3": "",
    "player_hint_1_en": "Let's start by penciling in (G)'s squares. She was beside a bed, but CANNOT be beside a plant since (E) is the only person beside a plant. She also CANNOT be in the last column since (C) is in that column. This should narrow down (G) to three squares – all of which are on a carpet. And per the general clue that only one person is on a carpet, we know that (G) is that person. Cross out all other carpet squares. We can also cross out R3 C1 because if someone were to occupy that square, that eliminates all the squares that (G) can occupy.",
    "player_hint_2_en": "Since (A) is beside a TV, he must be in R3, either C4 or C6. Cross out all other squares in that row. This narrows down (G) to be in R4 C1.",
    "player_hint_3_en": "Because (B) is on a bed, she has to be in C8. However, she CANNOT be in R1 C8 because (E) is the only person beside a plant, so (B) is in R2 C8.",
    "player_hint_4_en": "Amongst all the remaining chairs, (H) has to occupy R5 C3 because all the other chairs are beside a plant, which only (E) can be beside. (F) will be in R1 C4 since that's the last square for him to be beside a shelf. This narrows down (A) to R3 C6.",
    "player_hint_5_en": "(E) will occupy R7 C7 to be beside a plant. (D) is in R6 C2 to be beside the table. Because (C) is in the last column, she must be in R9 C9.",
    "player_hint_6_en": "This leaves the last square R8 C5 for (V) – hence (E) is the murderer."
  },
